      "body": "Do this once, before you add products. A few minutes here saves a lot of correcting later.\r\n\r\n## Your business details\r\n\r\nUnder Settings → Organization, fill in your business name, address, phone and logo. These appear on\r\nthe invoices and receipts your customers receive, so use the details you want them to see.\r\n\r\n## Report emails\r\n\r\nThe same page has an **Email Reports** section. EzyCore emails the owner a **Daily sales digest** on\r\ndays you made sales, and — if Expiry Tracking is on — an **Expiry report** listing stock that has\r\nexpired or is about to. Each one has its own switch and its own send time, in your own timezone. Turn\r\noff what you don't read; the expiry dates on your stock stay correct either way.\r\n\r\n## Locations\r\n\r\nA location is anywhere you hold stock — a shop, a warehouse, a storeroom. Every business starts with\r\none. Add more only if you genuinely keep stock in more than one place.\r\n\r\nLocations matter more than they first appear:\r\n\r\n- Stock counts are **per location**. A product can have 12 in the shop and 40 in the warehouse.\r\n- Sales and purchases apply to whichever location you are working in. The location picker is in the\r\n  top bar — check it before recording anything.\r\n- Stock by Location shows every product across every location on one screen.\r\n\r\nIf you only ever have one location, you can safely ignore all of this.\r\n\r\n## Turn features on and off\r\n\r\n**Feature Settings** controls how much of EzyCore you see. Turning a feature off hides it from the\r\nmenu entirely, which is the fastest way to make the app simpler for your staff.\r\n\r\nFeatures worth deciding on early:\r\n\r\n| Feature | Turn it on if |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Sales Management** | You sell from this system, not just track stock. Most businesses want this. |\r\n| **Expiry Tracking** | You sell anything perishable — medicine, food, cosmetics. |\r\n| **Ecommerce Storefront** | You want a public online shop as well as your counter. |\r\n| Tax Management | You charge VAT or any tax on sales. |\r\n| Returns Management | Customers return goods, or you return goods to suppliers. |\r\n| Barcode System | You scan barcodes at the counter. |\r\n\r\n**Expiry Tracking** deserves particular thought: it lets you *track product expiry dates with batch\r\nmanagement and alerts*, and it changes how stock is recorded — every batch gets a date, and sales\r\nsell the oldest batch first. Turning it on later means your existing stock has no batch dates, so\r\ndecide before you load your opening stock. See\r\n[Catch stock before it expires](/help/expiry-tracking).\r\n\r\nYour subscription plan decides which features are available at all. Anything not in your plan shows\r\nas locked, with a link to change your plan.\r\n\r\n## Next\r\n\r\n[Add your products](/help/add-your-products)."
